LL-1a  SYMBOLIC: saddle set of the split-cubic exponent Phi(s)=w s^2 - i b/s
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
saddle equation: s^3 = -i*beta/(2 w); roots and actions:
  arg(s*) = -pi/6
     Phi(s*)/(w^(1/3) beta^(2/3)):  Re = 3*2**(1/3)/4   Im = -3*2**(1/3)*sqrt(3)/4   Im/Re = -sqrt(3)
  arg(s*) = pi/2
     Phi(s*)/(w^(1/3) beta^(2/3)):  Re = -3*2**(1/3)/2   Im = 0   Im/Re = 0
  arg(s*) = -5*pi/6
     Phi(s*)/(w^(1/3) beta^(2/3)):  Re = 3*2**(1/3)/4   Im = 3*2**(1/3)*sqrt(3)/4   Im/Re = sqrt(3)

Check: |Phi(s*)| common modulus 3*2^(-2/3) = 1.889882
Admissible (Re>0, decaying) pair sits at action phases -+pi/3  =>  |Im|/Re = sqrt(3) EXACTLY.
Third root has Re<0 (growing e^{+c w^(1/3)}): Stokes-excluded for a Laplace transform
of a locally integrable one-sided density (transform must decay in Re w > 0).
on-shell Phi''(s*) = 6*w  (= 6w exactly, beta-independent fluctuation)

